---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Stories from '../components/Stories.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import img from '../assets/tamila-aspen-portrait.jpg';
import son from '../assets/gallery/military-family.jpg';
import { stories } from '../data/site.js';

const faq = [
  ['How much do I need for a down payment with a VA loan?', 'Eligible borrowers can buy with 0% down. Tamila checks your eligibility and explains the funding fee and closing costs up front.'],
  ['Can I buy before I arrive in Colorado?', 'Yes. Tamila has helped buyers who toured on short visits and closed while still living in another state. Video tours and electronic signing make it possible.'],
  ['I have PCS orders and need to sell. Can you help?', 'Yes. Tamila prices your home to sell on your timeline and can handle the sale after you have already left.'],
  ['Does the house need to be in good condition for a VA loan?', 'VA loans have minimum property requirements. Tamila checks the home early so repairs do not surprise you right before closing.'],
  ['Is there a limit on how much I can borrow with a VA loan?', 'If you have full entitlement, the VA sets no loan limit, as long as you can afford the payment and the appraisal supports the price (VA.gov). If part of your entitlement is still tied to another VA loan, a county limit applies to the zero-down amount. Tamila checks your Certificate of Eligibility and tells you exactly where you stand.'],
  ['Who does not pay the VA funding fee?', 'Veterans who receive VA compensation for a service-connected disability, those rated eligible for it (including from a pre-discharge exam), active-duty Purple Heart recipients and eligible surviving spouses. For other first-time users with no down payment, the fee is 2.15% of the loan and can be added to the loan.'],
  ['Do disabled veterans get a property tax break in Colorado?', 'Yes. Veterans rated 100% permanently disabled by the VA, or granted individual unemployability, can have 50% of the first $200,000 of their home\'s actual value exempted from property tax. Apply to your county assessor by July 1 of the year you want the exemption (Colorado Division of Property Taxation).'],
  ['I moved out of Colorado on orders. Will tax be withheld when I sell my house?', 'Usually yes. When the seller\'s address is outside Colorado and the price is over $100,000, the title company withholds the lesser of 2% of the price or the net proceeds. It comes back as a credit on your Colorado tax return. Tamila builds it into your net sheet so there are no surprises.'],
  ['Do you work near military bases?', 'Yes, across the Denver metro and Colorado Springs, including near Buckley Space Force Base in Aurora, Fort Carson, Peterson and Schriever Space Force Bases, and the U.S. Air Force Academy.'],
];
---
<Base title="VA Loans in Denver & Colorado Springs, PCS | Tamila Aspen" description="VA loans in Denver and Colorado Springs with 0% down, PCS moves and buying from out of state. Tamila Aspen is a military mom, agent and VA loan officer." schema={[{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })) }]}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="VA loans in Denver & Colorado Springs · Military relocation training"
    title="VA Loans and PCS Moves, From a Military Mom"
    lead="Tamila's son serves in the U.S. Air Force. She knows what orders, deployments and short timelines mean for a family, and she handles both the home and the VA loan."
    image={img}
    imageAlt="Tamila Aspen, VA loan officer and real estate agent"
    cta2={['#contact', 'Talk about my move']}
  />

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap mom">
      <Image src={son} alt="Tamila Aspen with her son Alexey in his U.S. Air Force uniform" widths={[360, 560]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 80vw, 380px" class="mom__img" />
      <div class="prose mom__text">
        <h2>Why This Matters to Tamila</h2>
        <p>When your family serves, moving is part of life. Tamila has lived it as a mother. She understands report dates, last-minute changes and buying a home from far away.</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><b>VA loans with 0% down</b> for eligible buyers, handled by Tamila herself as your loan officer.</li>
          <li><b>Buying from out of state</b> with video tours and electronic signing.</li>
          <li><b>Selling on PCS orders</b>, even after you have moved.</li>
          <li><b>VA property requirements</b> checked early, so repairs do not surprise you.</li>
          <li><b>Deployment-friendly scheduling</b>, seven days a week.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Near Colorado's Bases</h2>
      <p>Tamila helps military families across the Denver metro and Colorado Springs, including Aurora near Buckley Space Force Base, and Colorado Springs near Fort Carson, Peterson and Schriever Space Force Bases and the U.S. Air Force Academy.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Buckley Space Force Base, Aurora:</b> families often look in <a href="/areas/aurora">Aurora</a>, <a href="/areas/centennial">Centennial</a>, <a href="/areas/parker">Parker</a> and Denver. Compare <a href="/blog/aurora-vs-centennial">Aurora vs Centennial</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Fort Carson, Peterson and Schriever, and the Air Force Academy:</b> see the <a href="/areas/colorado-springs">Colorado Springs area guide</a> and <a href="/blog/colorado-springs-vs-monument-military-families">Colorado Springs vs Monument for military families</a>.</li>
        <li><b>Anywhere else on the Front Range:</b> Tamila also helps VA buyers in Greenwood Village, Highlands Ranch, Castle Rock, Littleton, Lakewood and the cities in between, and she can write VA loans anywhere in Colorado.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section mist">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>VA Loan Facts for Colorado Buyers</h2>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><b>No VA loan limit with full entitlement.</b> If you have never used your benefit, or have restored it, the VA sets no maximum loan amount. What you can borrow depends on your income and the appraisal.</li>
        <li><b>The funding fee, or no fee at all.</b> Most first-time users with no down payment pay a 2.15% funding fee, which can be added to the loan. Veterans who receive VA disability compensation, active-duty Purple Heart recipients and eligible surviving spouses do not pay it.</li>
        <li><b>A Colorado property tax break for disabled veterans.</b> If the VA rates you 100% permanently disabled, or you have individual unemployability, 50% of the first $200,000 of your home's value is exempt from property tax. Apply to the county assessor by July 1.</li>
        <li><b>Minimum property requirements.</b> The VA appraiser checks that the home is safe and sound. Tamila looks at the home with those rules in mind before you make an offer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Your PCS Move, Step by Step</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Orders in hand: call Tamila.</b> She pulls your Certificate of Eligibility and gets you preapproved, so you know your budget before you look.</li>
        <li><b>Pick the area by your commute.</b> Tell her where you will report. She suggests neighborhoods and checks schools, HOA and metro district taxes for each home.</li>
        <li><b>Tour in person or by video.</b> Use a house-hunting trip if you have one. If not, Tamila walks the home on a live video call and points out what photos hide.</li>
        <li><b>Write an offer that fits your report date.</b> Inspection, appraisal and closing deadlines are set around your orders, with room for the VA appraisal.</li>
        <li><b>Close from anywhere.</b> Most documents can be signed electronically. If you cannot be at the closing table, a power of attorney may be an option; Tamila and the title company plan it with you early.</li>
        <li><b>Selling the home you are leaving?</b> Tamila can sell it after you have moved. If you sell after you have left Colorado, plan for the 2% state withholding, which you get back as a tax credit.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btns"><a class="pill" href="/cost-to-sell-a-house-in-colorado">What you will net from your sale</a><a class="pill pill--line" href="/mortgage-calculator">VA payment calculator</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.va.gov/housing-assistance/home-loans/loan-limits/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">VA.gov: VA home loan limits</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.veteransunited.com/valoans/va-funding-fee-explains-the-fee-who-pays-what-and-why/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Veterans United: VA funding fee rates and exemptions</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://dpt.colorado.gov/property-tax-exemption-for-veterans-with-a-disability-and-gold-star-spouses" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Colorado Division of Property Taxation: Exemption for veterans with a disability</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://tax.colorado.gov/sites/tax/files/documents/DR1083_2025.pdf" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Colorado Department of Revenue: DR 1083, withholding on real property sales</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Stories items={[stories[2]]} title="Buying from another state" />
  <Faq items={faq} title="VA and PCS Questions" />
  <ContactBand title="Got Orders? Let's Make a Plan." lead="Tell Tamila your report date and what you need. She will call you back, usually the same day." goal="VA loan / PCS move" />
</Base>
<style>
  .mom { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: 48px; align-items: center; }
  .mom > * { min-width: 0; }
  .mom :global(.mom__img) { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3/4; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 24px; }
  .mom__text { margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .mom { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; } .mom :global(.mom__img) { max-width: 340px; margin-inline: auto; } }
</style>
